  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 225 AM CDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\nThe passage of a rather notable fall front is beginning to focus on \nThursday, as the midweek system begins to accelerate to the \nnortheast across the Plains. Rain and embedded thunder/lightning \npotential may continue through much of the day on Thursday, slowly\nabating from north-to-south after nightfall. It is likely that \nour current forecast highs on Thursday continue to tumble (esp. \nacross the northern one-half of Oklahoma) as a more refined\nfrontal timing, and degree of post-frontal rain and clouds, comes\ninto clearer view.\n\nThings turn drier and begin to feel more \"classically fall\" by \nFriday into the weekend, with daytime temperatures in the 60s \nbecoming more probable.\n\nUngar",
